Injection points for the port's tests, under the names of three of Apache
Cloudberry's faults inside PostgreSQL's own abort and checkpoint, which
distributed_transactions and pg_rewind_fail_missing_xlog in its isolation2
schedule set: an error in an abort once the transaction has ended for the
other backends, which has AbortTransaction() run again -- the core series'
XactAbortAgainAfterEnd (O37) keeps the second run from recording the abort
again; a checkpoint held with its redo point reckoned and its buffers
written, its record not yet, so that a node stopped there never completes
it; and a checkpoint held once its record is written and the control file
updated, before the WAL it no longer needs is removed:

  abort_after_procarray_end          xact.c, AbortTransaction()
  checkpoint_after_redo_calculated   xlog.c, CreateCheckPoint()
  checkpoint_control_file_updated    xlog.c, CreateCheckPoint()

gp_core's fault injector attaches a fault of Cloudberry's name to the point
(gp_fault.c).  They serve tests alone, so they are not in the core series:
Dockerfile.pg applies this after test-iso2-locks.patch, to the tree of
either ref, vanilla or patched, so that the two images still differ only in
the ref.  Dormant, as any point is: without injection points the macro is
empty, and with them a point nothing attached to runs no callback.


